{"name":"Bonfire Toffee","hex":"#d7af7a","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonfire toffee","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hard and brittle toffee associated with Halloween and Guy Fawkes Night (or Bonfire Night)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonfire_toffee"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonfire toffee","blocks":[{"text":"Bonfire toffee is a hard, brittle toffee associated with Halloween and Guy Fawkes Night in the United Kingdom. The toffee tastes very strongly of black treacle (molasses), and cheap versions can be quite bitter. In Scotland, the treat is known as claggum, with less sweet versions known as clack. In Wales, it is known as loshin du."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/BonfireToffee.jpg/330px-BonfireToffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonfire_toffee"},{"title":"Bonfire","blocks":[{"text":"A bonfire is a large and controlled outdoor fire, used for waste disposal or as part of a religious feast, such as Saint John's Eve."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg/330px-Seurasaari-2005-johannus2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonfire"},{"title":"Toffee","blocks":[{"text":"Toffee is an English confection made by caramelizing sugar or molasses along with butter, and occasionally flour. The mixture is heated until its temperature reaches the hard crack stage of 149 to 154 °C. While being prepared, toffee is sometimes mixed with nuts or raisins."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f3/Thorntonstoffee.jpg/330px-Thorntonstoffee.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toffee"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d2/Bonfire_2018%